silk-embroidered-suit/01.webp"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-2","ratio":"portrait","shot":"on_model_drape","alt":"Three-quarter view showing the fall of the drape: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":4500,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/02.webp"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-3","ratio":"portrait","shot":"on_model_detail","alt":"Close view of the border against the body: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":4500,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/03.jpg"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-4","ratio":"portrait","shot":"on_model_movement","alt":"The piece in movement, mid-turn: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":4500,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/04.webp"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-5","ratio":"portrait","shot":"flat_lay","alt":"The piece laid flat, folded to show body, border and pallu: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":4500,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/05.webp"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-6","ratio":"square","shot":"detail_weave","alt":"Macro detail of the weave: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":3000,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/06.webp"},{"id":"baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit-7","ratio":"square","shot":"detail_weave","alt":"Macro detail of the weave: sand beige kurta set in hand-embroidered tussar silk with floral motifs","width":3000,"height":3000,"src":"/reference-only/products/baluka-beige-tussar-silk-embroidered-suit/07.webp"}],"narrative":"Baluka is sand, and the piece is built in three layers of it. A plain inner kurta, a churidar in a lighter weight, and over both an embroidered overlay in raw tussar that carries the whole of the ornament. Keeping the worked surface on a layer that comes off is a practical decision as much as a designed one — it makes one set read as two, and it puts the hand-embroidery where it can be seen against the light rather than flat against the body.","spec":{"colour":"Sand beige","technique":"Hand-embroidered overlay over a plain inner kurta","fabric":"Raw tussar silk overlay, lighter silk inner","speciality":"Three pieces — overlay, inner kurta and churidar","note":"The overlay is the worked layer; the inner kurta is deliberately plain."},"provenance":{"workshop":"Sarnath atelier","loom":"Pit loom, tussar ground","weaveTimeWeeks":7,"artisanCount":5},"garmentType":"suit","fabric":"tussar-silk","colourFamily":"off-white","zariTypes":["resham"],"motifs":["floral","jaal"]}}],null]}],"$L27"]}]}]
